ing, you choose whether to harm or Kiss. And again: with multiple attack actions, can you drink multiple times in one turn or combine lashes to harm and lashes to drink?<br /> <br /> 4) Revelations of Midgard 3: the text says &quot;This power is always activated as the final action of a turn, after Celerity actions.&quot; Does it mean that at the end of every turn, regardless of how many actions I have done (following the rules of Multiple Actions and/or Celerity), I can choose to spend 1 blood point and roll Willpower at difficulty 6 (so, no penalty for multiple actions) to attract the blood? Basically this would mean the power is activated reflexively, but the text does not say that, though it would be consistent with the first two powers of this way being activated reflexively as well. Or is this power activated with the usual penalties for multiple actions (so it can't be activated if the difficulty goes to 10)? That would be interesting because my Narrator (or rather, the other players, since he deferred to their vote) ruled that Thaumaturgy (and other discipline powers which are not reflexive) cannot be activated as part of multiple actions - a decision I disagreed with.<br /> <br /> 5) Revelations of Duat 3 to 5: does the &quot;zombie&quot; obey a single edict pronounced by the Setite at the moment of its creation for the rest of its existence, regardless of which power is used? Then the proto-Bane mummies are limited to one edict, but it can be a complex one given the possibility to raise Intelligence. Or can new edicts be issued as long as the &quot;zombie&quot; exists, and the level of the power used only changes the complexity of the possible edicts? Or does it work in some other way?<br /> <br /> The Narrator and I have been having some differing views on how certain rules work (this edition's system is sort of new for both of us, who have played previous editions). If I can get clarity on these ones, I can present a clear and well-argumented interpretation of them before I spend xp for them and see if him and I can see eye to eye for greater comfort, otherwise I will have to go with what he understands or the other players vote. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}